const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文讨论如何利用 PE 和 PEG 比率估计权益资本的隐含预期回报率。 阅读时应把它理解为受样本、时点和制度限定的问题，而不是可以脱离条件的结论。",en:"The article considers how PE and PEG ratios can be used in estimating an implied expected rate of return on equity capital. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/accr.2004.79.1.73",label:{zh:"The Accounting Review (2004) · 来源说明",en:"The Accounting Review (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它通过价格、收益、增长预期和隐含预期回报的估值关系展开，而不把比率当作自解释指标。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中一项，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It works through valuation relationships that connect price, earnings, growth expectations, and an implied expected return, rather than treating a ratio as self-interpreting. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/accr.2004.79.1.73",label:{zh:"The Accounting Review (2004) · 来源说明",en:"The Accounting Review (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"可比输入需要时点价格、收益定义、增长假设或预测、稀释与股数处理、财年日期和原始样本过滤。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原研究分别记录，不能仅因变量同名或使用最新修订值就视为可比。",en:"Comparable inputs need point-in-time prices, earnings definitions, growth assumptions or forecasts, dilution and share-count treatment, fiscal dates, and the original sample filters. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/accr.2004.79.1.73",label:{zh:"The Accounting Review (2004) · 来源说明",en:"The Accounting Review (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"标题支持依赖模型的隐含预期回报练习，不意味着高低 PE 或 PEG 单独给出估值或收益结论。 它只支持来源所描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The title supports a model-dependent implied expected-return exercise; it does not make a low or high PE or PEG a stand-alone valuation or return conclusion. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/accr.2004.79.1.73",label:{zh:"The Accounting Review (2004) · 来源说明",en:"The Accounting Review (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"明确历史或前瞻收益、预测版本、负或接近零收益处理、货币、公司行动，以及所用方程和期限。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Specify trailing versus forward earnings, forecast vintage, negative or near-zero earnings treatment, currency, corporate actions, and the equation and horizon used. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/accr.2004.79.1.73",label:{zh:"The Accounting Review (2004) · 来源说明",en:"The Accounting Review (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Accounting Review (2004)。比率对会计和预期输入敏感，不能作为实时信号、目标价或权益资本成本保证。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Accounting Review (2004). Ratios are sensitive to accounting and expectation inputs, so this framework is not a live signal, target price, or assurance of equity cost of capital. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/accr.2004.79.1.73",label:{zh:"The Accounting Review (2004) · 来源说明",en:"The Accounting Review (2004) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“PE Ratios, PEG Ratios, and Estimating the Implied Expected Rate of Return on Equity Capital”公开说明的研究对象与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。比率对会计和预期输入敏感，不能作为实时信号、目标价或权益资本成本保证。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “PE Ratios, PEG Ratios, and Estimating the Implied Expected Rate of Return on Equity Capital”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
